Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Amend Addenda  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Breast  excisional tissue  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  JAMES D IGLEHART M D   CASE  BS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME              Addended Report              Resident  Alison Z Young  M D   Ph D   Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  poorly differentiated  modified Bloom Richardson  grade III III   0 3cm  is present in an area of radiologic calcifications in  the upper inner quadrant  slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The carcinoma appears to be in an area  of prior treated tumor   No lymphovascular invasion is seen   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  solid type  high nuclear grade  is present as  multiple foci within areas of the tumor bed in the upper inner quadrant   including the areas associated with two clips placed by core needle biopsy and  with areas of radiologic calcifications  8 slides   DCIS is associated with  calcifications  No necrosis is seen   The deep margin is free of carcinoma   The skin and nipple are free of carcinoma   Two lymph nodes with no tumor seen  No evidence of prior tumor involvement is  seen   Note  The patient presented with 4 5cm poorly differentiated ductal carcinoma  and had a negative sentinel lymph node  She is now s p treatment   After treatment  the mass was no longer palpable  A 0 5cm irregular mass was  identified by ultrasound  Mammography showed two clips and pleomorphic  calcifications in the upper inner quadrant  MRI showed a marked response  but  with residual clumped linear enhancement   The mastectomy was radiographed to identify the two clips and two areas of  calcifications  A 0 7cm irregular stellate area is identified grossly  which  correlates with tumor bed and residual DCIS  However  tumor bed changes and  DCIS are also present in adjacent tissue  surrounding the areas of the clips  and the radiologic calcifications  in an area measuring 4 to 5cm in size   The residual invasive carcinoma is similar in appearance to the pre treatment  carcinoma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    but is less cellular  The carcinoma appears viable and  mitotic figures are present  Immunohistochemical studies will be repeated and  reported in an addendum  The residual DCIS consists of scattered and focally  clustered markedly pleomorphic cells in ducts   This would be considered a Miller Payne Grade 4 response   CLINICAL DATA   History  38 year old female with  R  breast carcinoma  s p chemo  carboplatin   Taxotere  Herceptin   negative sentinal lymph node bx   Operation  Right simple mastectomy   Operative Findings  None given   Clinical Diagnosis  Right breast cancer   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Right simple mastectomy   stitch on lower axillary node   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number   and  Right simple mastectomy   stitch on lower axillary node   and consists of  a REMOVED_DATE gm simple mastectomy specimen  16 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm   with a tan  wrinkled skin ellipse  14 6 x 7 2cm    The tan nipple  1 3cm in greatest  dimension  is everted with focal purple gray discoloration  The areola   3 5cm in greatest dimension  is tan brown  No scar is grossly identified on  the epithelial surface  Per surgeon  there is a stitch designating the  lower  axillary node   The deep margin  inked black  is a smooth fascial plane  The  specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral  and is radiographed per  prosector in the surgical pathology cutting room  In the central superior  breast  approximately 12 o clock   there is an irregular poorly delineated firm  white fibrous area  0 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm   3 4cm superior deep to the nipple and  1 8cm from the deep margin  This area was previously sampled by the tissue  bank in the frozen section room  1 6cm inferior anterior to the  aforementioned firm fibrous area a clip  designated as clip 1 on radiograph  is  identified within a poorly delineated indurated pink white lesion  0 6 x REMOVED_DATE x  0 5cm   in the central breast  2 4cm from the nipple and 3 6cm from the deep  margin  The lesion exhibits peripheral hemorrhage as consistent with prior  core biopsy procedure and clip placement  Approximately 1 8cm medial inferior  to the clip 1 lesion  in the upper inner quadrant  approximately 2 o clock    the second clip  designated as clip 2 on the radiograph  is identified  Clip 2  is associated with a poorly delineated pink white lesion  0 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm     The clip 2 lesion is 1 6cm deep to the skin and 3 8cm from the deep margin   In the upper inner quadrant  and focally in the lower inner quadrant   approximately REMOVED_DATE o clock  there are multiple punctate scattered calcifications  in the specimen radiograph  The remaining breast is composed of approximately  70  yellow tan lobulated adipose tissue with approximately 30  focally dense to  lumpy tan white fibrous stroma   The most lateral aspect of the specimen  slice 10  is examined for lymph node  candidates  Two axillary lymph node candidates  1 2cm and 1 8cm in greatest  dimension  are identified  the largest of which corresponds to the  aforementioned stitch   Representative sections to include the entire firm area previously sampled in  the frozen room  the clip 1 lesion  the clip 2 lesion  and per radiograph the  areas of punctate calcification are submitted as follows   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Previously sampled firm area approximately 12 o clock  2 frags  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Deep margin closest to previously sampled firm area  12 o clock  1  frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Clip 1 lesion sequentially submitted from lateral to medial  3  frags total  ESS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Deep margin over clip 1 lesion  2 frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Clip 2 lesion  entirely submitted from late