Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Neurology Assoc Wac 835 Path Subspecialty Service  Hemepath Results To  ALLAN ENRIQUE PINEDA  M D  MARGO M MOSKOS  M D  Resident  Joseph Gaut  M D   Ph D  Consulting Pathologist s   Judith A Ferry  M D  Signed Out by  Aliyah Rahemtullah  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Area  1  suspicious appearing lymph node at 10 o clock  no known breast CA at this time   Area  2  indeterminate lymph node area at 9 o clock  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  AREA  1  RIGHT  10 00   CORE BIOPSY  REACTIVE FOLLICULAR AND MONOCYTOID B CELL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY   SEE NOTE   BREAST  AREA  2  RIGHT  9 00   CORE BIOPSY  REACTIVE FOLLICULAR AND MONOCYTOID B CELL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Both core biopsies contain portions of intramammary lymph nodes with enlarged  reactive appearing germinal centers  intact mantle zones  and patent sinuses  The interfollicular areas contain small lymphocytes and increased numbers of monocytoid B cells adjacent to medullary sinuses  Focally  small clusters of epithelioid histiocytes are present surrounding one follicle  well formed granulomas  necrotic area or large cells are not identified  Breast parenchymal tissue is not present  Immunohistochemical stains demonstrate that  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   B cells are present mainly confined to follicles  mantle zones  and areas rich in monocytoid B cells  with many small interfollicular  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   T cells  Germinal centers are bcl6    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and bcl2   and are encompassed by  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   intact and occasionally expanded follicular dendritic cell aggregates  A stain for Ki67 shows an appropriately high level of staining within reactive follicles  There is no staining of lymphoid cells with an antibody to cyclin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   In situ hybridization for kappa and lambda immunoglobulin light chains highlights polytypic plasma cells  The overall morphologic and immunophenotypic findings support a reactive process for the lymph node enlargement  but the specific etiology is uncertain  The presence of reactive follicular hyperplasia with increased monocytoid B cells and clusters of epithelioid histiocytes at least focally raises the possibility of toxoplasma associated lymphadenitis  Correlation with serologic studies may be informative  This immunoperoxidase test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  area  1  10 o clock   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled   area  2   are three cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Aliyah Rahemtullah M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM  ADDITIONAL IMMUNOHISTOCHEM