Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 01 CLINICAL DATA  Eighty five year old female with 2cm mass in left breast  FNA positive for cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY AND MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE WITH MUCIN PRODUCTION AND SIGNET RING CELLS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures approximately 2 5cm in greatest dimension  The inked resection margins are negative for carcinoma  There is no evidence of malignancy in 13 out of 13 lymph nodes  In areas the tumor has a colloid pattern  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  Virtually all of the tumor is infiltrating  however  there is one focus of severe ductal hyperplasia  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 18 15                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Estradiol receptor  Positive 66 femtomoles mg protein  Progestin receptor  Not determined  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 11     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY AND MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   6   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section laboratory is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a 1 3cm rubbery nodule on one edge obliterating the resection margin  inked and sectioned to reveal the nodule to be ill defined  bulging  tan brown and focally red  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and submitted in A  The rest of the mass is submitted in B  Some tissue is saved for E R  studies  The remaining non frozen tissue is submitted entirely in C E  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  suture at apex of axilla  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a left breast  15 x 15 x 3 5cm  an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 9cm skin ellipse  and 7 x 4 x 2 5cm axillary tail  The entire specimen weighs 415 grams  A 3cm recent incision with sutures is present centrally 3cm away from the closest skin margin  Beneath this is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 3cm cavity containing fresh blood clot  The cavity is partially surrounded by 0 5cm thick firm  indurated  white tan mass at the posterior surface  grossly 1cm away from the deepest resection margin  In addition  a 4 x 3 x 2cm area inferior and adjacent to the cavity is tan yellow  hemorrhagic and focally firm  The remaining parenchyma is mostly yellow  lobulated with focal rubbery  white areas  The nipple  which is 0 5cm superior to the incision  does not have a pigmented areola  and is unremarkable  The axillary lymph nodes are white tan  focally firm  the largest being 0 9cm  Section Code F  representative sections of firm areas surrounding the cavity G H   representative sections of the hemorrhagic areas around the cavity I   deepest resection margin J L   other deep resection margin