tain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 15     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two specimens  Labeled  left breast  medial  palpable lesion   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm fibroadipose tissue fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal a fatty cut surface with white fibrous tissue  but no areas suspicious for carcinoma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through E  Labeled  left breast  lateral lesion   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibroadipose tissue fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal a fatty cut surface with areas of white  rubbery  shiny tissue  Fragment is entirely submitted in F through L  Resident  DARRYL E  PAL