Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 15 CLINICAL DATA  Nodule by mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 46 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm hard tan pink nodule on an inked margin too small to freeze  Nodule is submitted in cassettes A and B  the remainder of the tissue is in cassettes C through F  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX  LEFT BREAST   LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
