Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  A   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  65   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location  MGH  RADIOLOGY  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 08 55  Results To   Matthew W Colman MD      FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   Chest wall mass  biopsy     High grade malignant neoplasm  most consistent with a high grade sarcoma  grade  2 of 3  See note     Note   The biopsy shows markedly atypical spindle shaped cells  Focally  epithelioid  cells are also present  On immunohistochemistry the epithelioid cells are  positive for keratin  wide spectrum   and negative for keratin  cocktail  and  EMA  The neoplastic cells are diffusely positive for desmin  and focally  positive for actin  Immunohistochemical stains for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   myogenin and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are  negative     The presence of epithelioid cells and keratin reactivity raises the possibility  of a sarcomatoid carcinoma  However  the overall morphological appearance  in  conjunction with the clinical features  is indicative of a high grade sarcoma   likely related to the prior use of radiation therapy  Dr  Melinda Lerwill from  the Breast service has reviewed selected slides and concurs with this opinion            Electronically Signed Out By Vikram Deshpande MBBS           By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       CLINICAL HISTORY  History of right breast cancer 30 years ago     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  CHEST WALL MASS BIOPSY  RIGHT ANTERIOR    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PAT