Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 42 CLINICAL DATA  Nodule at previous excision site for breast masses  2   excised on REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE Persistent mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  BOTH FRAGMENTS  EACH WITH A MAXIMUM TUMOR DIMENSION OF REMOVED_DATE CM   NOTE  Most of the specimen consists of infiltrating carcinoma  Multiple resection margins are involved  No normal breast tissue is present  nor is there an in situ component away from the invasive areas  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  The previous biopsies   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   are reviewed  and no tumor is identified in either  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 08     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 10 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragments of white  smooth  rubbery  focally fatty breast tissue  The pieces are inked and sectioned with one half of each frozen as frozen section  1  now A  The remainder in B  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  S