redictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place  no microcalcifications seen on the x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 3cm firm  tan stellate area grossly suspicious for carcinoma but too small to freeze  Submitted entirely in A through G  with suspicious area in C and D  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast cyst  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse overlying a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm relatively thin walled cyst that is filled with dark brown thick material  The skin surface shows a less than 0 1cm in diameter ulceration  The specimen is resected and submitted entirely in AA  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST MASS   VERY SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  NO FROZEN SECTION PERFORMED  AT REQUEST OF SURGEON  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST MASS PART B  LEFT BREAST CYST   report_end  , Yes.
