Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 52 CLINICAL DATA  Abnormal density right mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY    INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 1 2 3   REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AND APPROACHING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED SURGICAL MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  There is no in situ component identified  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  Receptor studies will be done on the formalin fixed tissue and reported separately  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with localizing wire in place  An x ray accompanies this specimen which indicates microcalcifications  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm stellate nodule REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in the center of the specimen which approaches to within 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through F  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION  GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS LESION TOO SMALL FOR HORMOME BINDING ASSAY  AWAIT PERMANENT  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , No.
