 RIGHT  MASS  AND  SUPERO LATERAL  SPECIMENS   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  BREAST  RIGHT   LATERAL  SPECIMEN   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue containing a pink tan firm nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The nodule is well demarcated and is present within 0 1cm to the closest inked margin  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  The remainder of the breast tissue is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections from the specimen are submitted in cassettes A th