specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white stellate firm lesion subjacent to the epidermal scar and 0 5cm from the designated 12 o clock margin and 0 9cm from the posterior margin  The remaining parenchyma contains a moderate amount of tan white firm  dense fibrous tissue which appears to extend to multiple inked margins including the posterior  This is admixed with approximately 40  tan yellow lobular fat  Within the dense white fibrous tissue a few purple firm cysts averaging REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Stellate lesion to posterior  B D  Stellate lesion to skin and anterior 12 o clock margin  E  Representative section of cyst  F  Representative section of parenchyma at the 9 o clock margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast and axillary resection   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm simple mastectomy with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 8cm wrinkled tan skin ellipse containing an eccentric 4 0cm nipple areolar complex and a 4 5cm well healed linear scar 1 5cm from the nipple areolar complex and 0 9cm from the closest skin margin  No orientation is given for the specimen so the deep margin is inked red  All other margins are inked black and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm biopsy cavity which has a surrounding  indurated border ranging from 0 1cm up to 1 5cm and consisting of bright yellow areas suggestive of fat necrosis and tan white firm stellate extensions projecting towards multiple margins  This biopsy cavity is 0 8cm from the posterior margin  0 8cm from the anterior margin closest to the epidermal scar  This is designated as 12 o clock  The remaining parenchyma consists of approximately 80  tan yellow lobular fat admixed with approximately 10  tan white firm dense fibrous tissue  No other lesions are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  G H  Biopsy cavity to posterior margin  I  Biopsy cavity to closest anterior 12 o clock margin  J  Biopsy cavity to skin  K L  Representative sections away from biopsy cavity  6 o clock   Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan yellow lobular aggregate containing multiple rubbery lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  Lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes  M O  Whole lymph nodes  P  Representative sections node  Gross Description by  KRISTEN SMITH Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS  LEFT    report_end  , No.
