f paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is an oriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm breast fragment with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 7cm firm and gritty  stellate  white mass which grossly abuts the superficial margin  The tumor is focally less than 0 1cm from the lateral margin  focally 0 3cm from the superior margin  and at least 0 4cm from the deep margin  Representative section of the tumor abutting the superficial margin is frozen as FX  1 and resubmitted in cassette A  The remainder of the tumor is submitted in cassettes B through D  with the superficial  deep  and superior margins demonstrated in B  deep margin demonstrated in C  and lateral margin in D   The superior aspect is overinked green  and the deep aspect overinked blue   A second 0 3cm firm  well circumscribed nodule is located medial to the mass  and is grossly cleared of all surrounding margins  submitted in cassette E  Representative section of uninvolved dense breast tissue is in cassette F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in 5 parts  labeled  add deep margin L breast  is an irregular 3 7x 2 7x 1 0cm fragment of primarily fatty unremarkable tissue  most of which is submitted in cassettes G and H  Labeled  final shave L breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 