Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  UpdatedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Nash  Jennifer Reports To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  History of invasive ductal and lobular carcinoma  Bow tie stitches in new cephalad  Short stitch   anterior  long stitch   lateral  posterior aspect in biopsy cavity is open  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  SPANNING 1 2CM X 1 1CM  GLASS SLIDE MEASUREMENT   ALL RESECTION MARGINS ARE NEGATIVE   0 2CM   SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 1  SMALL FOCI WITHIN THE TUMOR  ALL RESECTION MARGINS ARE NEGATIVE   0 2CM   LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   EXTENSIVE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OUT OF 17 LYMPH NODES WHICH MEASURES 1MM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AND IS IDENTIFIED BOTH ON AN HE AND A CYTOKERATIN IMMUNOSTAIN  NO EXTRACAPSULAR LYMPHATIC EXTENSION IS IDENTIFIED  NOTE  This tumor is arising in the vicinity of the nipple and is not immediately adjacent to the biopsy cavity  The carcinoma extends into the deep dermis of the nipple  with focal pagetoid spread into the epidermis  Paget s Disease of the breast   In this region  tumor is also present within lymphatic vessels  with focal perineural invasion  When comparing this carcinoma with the patient s previous ductal and lobular carcinomas   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    the current tumor is not morphologically identical to either  This histologic discrepancy  in addition to the small foci of ductal carcinoma in situ identified within the tumor  and the fact that the tumor is not immediately next to the previous biopsy site  all raise the possibility that this tumor may represent a third primary  The invasive carcinoma is positive for e cadherin  which is consistent with an invasive ductal carcinoma  There is no evidence of residual invasive lobular carcinoma  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  There are several cellular proliferations within the ducts in this specimen   the cells of which show negative staining with an e cadherin stain  supporting that these proliferations are lobular carcinoma in situ rather than ductal carcinoma in situ  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen  Along the anterior surface is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm flattened and slightly indurated nipple  Located 2 5cm superior to the nipple is a well healed linear scar measuring 6 5cm in length  The remaining skin surface is pink white and unremarkable  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm attached axillary tail  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm previous biopsy cavity within the mid portion of the specimen coming to 2 9cm from the overlying unremarkable free moving posterior aspect  4 5cm from the blue inked anterior soft tissue margin and 4 2cm from the scar bearing overlying skin  The cavity is empty and has a dark red to pink  smooth glistening cavity lining  The cavity borders are rubbery with focal areas of fat necrosis  No masses are grossly appreciated  Surrounding the cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm area of dense lobulated pink white fibrous tissue  The remaining parenchyma is tan yellow to pink lobulated and unremarkable with no additional masses or lesions identified  Adjacent to the nipple is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm smooth walled unilocular cystic structure surrounded by slightly indurated fibrous tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm    Within the attached axillary tail  multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in maximum dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of posterior margin closest to cavity taken en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavity wall   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved surrounding dense fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of nipple with cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Four whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One whole lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional axillary fat  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of nipple and surrounding fibrous tissue  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of gray to tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the anterior  a long black stitch the lateral  and a bow tie stitch the cephalad margins  The posterior aspect is inked black  the anterior is blue  the superior is green and the inferior is yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm gray pink fibrous  hemorrhagic cavity which communicates with the posterior margin  The cavity is surrounded by abundant chalky tan yellow areas consistent with fat necrosis  Within the cavity wall along the medial half of the specimen is a silver metal clip  A second staple is noted along the mid to lateral portion of the specimen  The remaining cut surface shows dense  rubbery  gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  with the cavity as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and the tissue bearing the silver metal clips as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  ML 11  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  ML 11  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Hem Malignancies  YAW 7    Consulting Pathologist s   None  Assigned Resident Path  Anthony J Iafrate  M D   Ph D   Clinical History  Erythrocytosis and macrocytosis    Reports To   DAVID B SYKES  M D         FINAL DIAGNOSIS     TEST PERFORMED    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID G T   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mutation Analysis    INDICATION FOR TEST   Erythrocytosis and macrocytosis    RESULTS    NEGATIVE  no  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  c  REMOVED_CASE_ID G T   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   mutant allele extension product peak was  detected when testing DNA from the patient s blood specimen  The wild type  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   c  REMOVED_CASE_ID G extension product peak was detected     INTERPRETATION   Published reports indicate the presence of the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  mutation is evidence  supporting a diagnosis of a chronic myeloproliferative disorder  namely  Polycythemia Vera  Essential Thrombocythemia or Idiopathic Myelofibrosis     COMMENT  A low tumor burden  less than 2 in 100 cells with heterozygous  mutation in the peripheral blood  may result in a false negative result     TEST INFORMATION   A recurrent point mutation in the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  kinase  exon 14  c  REMOVED_CASE_ID G T   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    has  been found in a majority of Polycythemia Vera cases  and a subset of Essential  Thrombocythemia and Idiopathic Myelofibrosis  Agnogenic Myeloid Metaplasia   cases  The identification of this mutation has diagnostic utility and has not  been found in normal or reactive conditions  It is rarely found in other  myeloproliferative disorders  We have developed a single base extension assay   SNaPshot  to genotype c  REMOVED_CASE_ID  in the forward and reverse directions from  genomic DNA samples from blood  bone marrow or splenectomies with  extramedullary hematopoiesis specimens  The analytic sensitivity of detecting  the mutation has been established in our laboratory at approximately 1  mutant  allele frequency or 2  heterozygous mutant cells     Baxter  E  J   L  M  Scott  et al    REMOVED_CASE_ID     Acquired mutation of the tyrosine  kinase  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  in human myeloproliferative disorders   Lancet 365  REMOVED_CASE_ID    REMOVED_DATE  James  C   V  Ugo  et al    REMOVED_CASE_ID     A unique clonal  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  mutation leading to  constitutive signaling causes polycythaemia vera   Nature 434  REMOVED_CASE_ID    REMOVED_DATE  Kralovics  R   F  Passamonti  et al    REMOVED_CASE_ID     A gain of function mutation of   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  in myeloproliferative disorders   N Engl J Med 352 17   REMOVED_DATE  Levine  R  L   M  Wadleigh  et al    REMOVED_CASE_ID     Activating mutation in the tyrosine  kinase  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  in polycythemia vera  essential thrombocythemia  and myeloid  metaplasia with myelofibrosis   Cancer Cell 7 4   REMOVED_DATE  Zhao  R   S  Xing  et al    REMOVED_CASE_ID     Identification of an acquired  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  mutation  in polycythemia vera   J Biol Chem 280 24   REMOVED_DATE    This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Diagnostic Molecular Pathology Laboratory  It has not been cleared or  approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that  such clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical  purposes  Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has  established and verified the test s accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH internal address  Diagnostic Molecular Pathology  Laboratory  Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St   Warren 508  Boston   MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID          Final 