Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 03 CLINICAL DATA  Mass on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  LESION  1  BOTH SPECIMENS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY AND RE EXCISION  1  FOCAL DUCT ECTASIA  2  RARE FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  CYSTS  FIBROSIS  APOCRINE CHANGE  AND FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  3  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE GROSS INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  BREAST  RIGHT  LESION  2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  70    REMOVED_DATE CM IN MAXIMUM DIMENSION MEASURED FROM SLIDES  EXTENDING TO AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  30    PRESENT AT A DISTANCE FROM THE MAIN TUMOR MASS  AND PRESENT AT MARGINS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  FIBROSIS  CYSTS  AND FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA WITH LUMINAL MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  No lymphatic vessel or blood vessel invasion is identified  The gross intra operative impression is confirmed  Hormone receptor studies will be performed  and the results reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 56                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  LESION  2   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  are three parts  Labeled  Lesion  1  superior portion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast biopsy with no abnormalities  entirely submitted in A through J  Labeled  Lesion  1  re excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm breast biopsy with no abnormalities  entirely submitted in K through M  Labeled  Mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm breast biopsy containing 0 6cm firm mass approaching inked  the mass is entirely submitted in N  representative sections of the remaining tissue in O through R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT  1 AND REEXCISION   NO LESIONS GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  NO CALCIFICATIONS GROSSLY IDENTIFIED  NO FROZEN SECTION DONE  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT  2   LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D