e studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the  following results for invasive carcinoma  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Estrogen receptor POSITIVE  Progesterone receptor POSITIVE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu  c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NEGATIVE   HETEROGENEOUS  1    FISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER 2 DNA Probe Kit with  the following results  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Results  NOT AMPLIFIED  HER 2 CEP 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE  The average of HER 2 copies per cell  REMOVED_DATE  The average centromere 17 copies per cell  REMOVED_DATE  REFERENCE RANGE   NOT AMPLIFIED HER 2 CEP 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE  EQUIVOCAL HER 2 CEP 17 ratio REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE  AMPLIFIED  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CEP 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE  Immunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following  criteria   Hormone receptor analysis  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the  carcinoma is reported as follows   positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive  positive   low   0      10  of nuclei immunoreactive  negative 0  of nuclei immunoreactive  The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet  been determined    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu analysis   Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor  cells   Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but  only a portion of the membrane is positive   Equivocal  2   Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane  immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells   Positive  3   Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells   Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result   External controls are evaluated and show appropriate immunoreactivity   The immunoperoxidase  immunofluorescence and in situ hybridization