Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 12 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  ADDITIONAL TISSUE RECEIVED Revised by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Revised on 19 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 41                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  99    REMOVED_DATE CM AS MEASURED ON A HISTOLOGIC SLIDE  WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED EXTENDING TO LESS THAN ONE HIGH POWER FIELD OF MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  1    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES WITH FOCAL COMEDO NECROSIS  PRESENT LESS THAN ONE HIGH POWER FIELD OF SEVERAL INKED SURFACES  NOTE  SEVERAL FOCI ARE SUSPICIOUS BUT NOT DIAGNOSTIC FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION  THE TUMOR DISPLAYS FEATURES OF BOTH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA  MICROCALCIFICATIONS ARE ASSOCIATED WITH THE INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  ADDENDUM FOR ESTROGEN AND PROGESTERONE RECEPTORS TO FOLLOW  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 26                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 26                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  Simon Powell  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  MOUNT AUBURN HOSPITAL OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  Brinda R  Kamat  M D  MOUNT AUBURN HOSPITAL  PATHOLOGY  300 MOUNT AUBURN STREET CAMBRIDGE  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  OUTSIDE CLINICIAN  Marvin B  Corlette  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  30 AUG  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  4 Blocks  2   report_end  , No.
