Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 11 CLINICAL DATA  82 year old with calcifications in right and left breast on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFERIOR    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion is not seen  BREAST  RIGHT   SUPERIOR    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW TO HIGH GRADE  EXTENSIVE  HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN SEVERAL FOCI  MULTIPLE SMALL PAPILLOMAS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 05                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are two pieces of breast tissue  The first specimen is designated  Superior specimen left breast  and is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm breast tissue fragment  It is inked and sectioned to reveal numerous small cysts up to 0 3cm in greatest dimension  Fully submitted in formalin in A F  Labeled  Inferior specimen left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm breast tissue fragment  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 9cm white firm area with irregular borders suspicious for carcinoma  Sections for formalin are submitted in G through N  Cassettes H  I  and J include the suspicious sections  Fully submitted  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX  BREAST  INFERIOR LEFT   REMOVED_DATE CM NODULE SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LEFT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
