Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 10 36 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D   PRIVATE CONSUL Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 14 59                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  The histological appearance of this tumor suggests that it should stain for estrogen receptor protein  The lack of staining for estrogen receptor protein may represent a falsely negative result  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the corresponding values were 97  and 95   respectively  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 breast carcinomas with determination of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy nine percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 97  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 92 at 14 59                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE  CONSULT  REPORTS TO  Rebecca Ann Osgood  M D  OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  Rebecca Osgood  M D  DEPT  OF PATH  CAMBRIDGE HOSPITAL  REMOVED_CASE_ID  CAMBRIDGE ST  CAMBRIDGE  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  16 SEP  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  2 Blocks  2   report_end  , No.
