as 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Two specimens are received  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached axillary tail measuring REMOVED_DATE x 7 x 1 5cm and a suture  designating the superior aspect of the specimen  There is an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 14 9cm which contains a 2 0cm well healed  linear scar immediately lateral to an unremarkable nipple  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a stellate shaped area of tan white  rubbery parenchyma with a hemorrhagic central area measuring 0 5cm  and 2 5cm from the nearest  superior  margin  The area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and radiates to within 1 5cm of the nearest margin  superior  and 1 4cm from the deep margin  Separate from the area of the biopsy cavity by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm area of tan white  fibrous tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white  focally cystic  firm mass 2 5cm away from the nearest  anterior  margin  The remaining uninvolved areas of parenchyma contain scattered areas of rubbery  tan white nodularity  The axillary lymph nodes range in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm  SECTION CODE A  Nearest  anterior  margin  biopsy cavity  B E  Biopsy cavity  F H  Mass away from biopsy cavity  I  Nearest  anterior  margin  mass away from biopsy cavity  J K  Uninvolved parenchyma  L V  Axillary lymph nodes  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  lateral quadrant right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unremarkable skin ellipse  The deep portion of the specimen contains multiple cysts 3 0cm in greatest dimension  The cysts are smooth walled and filled with straw colored fluid  Further sectioning of the specimen reveals unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with focal areas of tan white rubbery nodularity  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes W through FF with sections of cystic areas in BB through DD  Gross Description by  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  CYSTS  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  LATERAL QUADRANT    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , No.
