Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Amend Addenda  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Soft tissue biopsy  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M D   CASE  BS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME              Addended Report              Resident  David Wu  M D   Pathologist  Janina A Longtine  M D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   A 1  LEFT BREAST TISSUE  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  Benign breast tissue and overlying skin with no tumor present  entire specimen  submitted    Focal lymphoid infiltrate composed predominantly of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive T cells and  fewer  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive B cells  non specific  B 2  LEFT AXILLARY NODES  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  NON HODGKIN LYMPHOMA  B CELL SUBTYPE  see NOTE  The lymph node is expanded and at low power is mottled with zones of pale  cells  The cells within these zones are primarily small lymphocytes that are   monocytoid  in appearance admixed with scattered large lymphocytes and  occasional Reed Sternberg like cells  The infiltrate extends into extranodal  fat   Immunohistochemistry performed at BWH reveals the lymphoid population is  composed of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive B cells with admixed smaller population of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  positive T cells   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  highlights frequent expanded  serpiginous  follicular dendritic meshwork  The pale zones appear to surround these  follicular dendritic network   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is present in lymphocytes associated with  the follicles  Strong BCL 2 and weak BCL 6 staining is present throughout   No apparent preferential light chain immunoglobulin staining is seen  No  definitive preferential heavy chain immunoglobulin expression is seen  IgG   IgM  IgA   Distorted germinal center B cells are highlighted by IgD  immunostaining   A proliferative index as assessed by MIB 1 immunostaining is low with  approximately 5 10  positivity of the overall cellularity and is associated  with the follicles   Flow cytometric analysis   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   performed at BWH revealed within the  lymphocyte gate  approximately 65  of the cells are T cells expressing mature T  cell markers and 40  of the cells are B cells with polyclonal surface  immunoglobulin expression   Molecular diagnostic studies show a clonal immunoglobulin heavy chain gene  rearrangement  see  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Cytogenetic analysis reveals a complex karyotype   51 X  X der 1 add 1  p36 ins 1    q21     3 i 3  p10  t 3 4  q2 7 q12     5 i 5  p10  del 6  q21q23   9  11 add 11  q2 3  dup 12  q13q24   18  21  mar c  p6   49 idem  del 6  q21q23   add 11  q23  cp2  46 XX 2   See  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    NOTE  The overall findings are consistent with involvement by a NON HODGKIN  LYMPHOMA  B CELL SUBTYPE  morphologically most in keeping with a nodal marginal  zone lymphoma  The morphologic features and MIB 1 index suggest that the  lymphoma is low grade  despite the complex karyotype   This case was reviewed at BWH Hematopathology Staff Consensus Conference on  5 15 08  with concurrence   CLINICAL DATA   History  85 year old woman with 5cm left axillary mass  S P no diagnostic  core    erythema and skin thickening of breast  Rule out metastatic breast  cancer vs lymphoma   Operation  Left axillary node sampling  left breast incisional biopsy   Operative Findings  Not provided   Clinical Diagnosis  Left axillary mass   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  L breast tissue with skin  perm    B 2  L axillary nodes   assessment of tissue for lymphoma   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh in two parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s  name  and medical record number   Part A is sublabeled   1  Left breast tissue with skin  perm    and consists of  a REMOVED_DATE g breast excisional specimen  7 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm   with an overlying  tan pink skin ellipse  6 2 x 2 0cm    The specimen is received inked by the  surgeon  The inking is different from pathology protocol  surgeon contacted   superior red  inferior green  posterior black  lateral orange  medial yellow    The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely from lateral  orange   to medial  yellow    Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast tissue  multi frags  ESS   Part B is sublabeled   2  Left axillary mass   and consists of a tan brown mass   9 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm   that is composed of lobulated fleshy multiple nodules  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 8cm with focal necrosis and hemorrhage   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the mass in B   1 frag  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the mass  multi frags  RSS   Representative sections of the mass are submitted for flow cytogenetics   molecular and touch prep x5   QY lp  CASE NUMBER  BS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Janina A Longtine M D   Electronically signed on  5 29  REMOVED_CASE_ID   ADDENDUM   For clarity  there was no preferential expression of either kappa or lambda  immunoglobulin light chains by immunohistochemistry  The diagnosis is  unchanged   Addendum  1 by Janina A Longtine M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE   report_end  , No.
