Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Molecular Pathology Report  MYC FISH      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  M   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  66   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  YAW 7  GI CC  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 12 12  Results To   John T Mullen MD  Amy Ly MD    CLINICAL HISTORY   Soft Tissue  Left Breast Areola  Angiosarcoma    SPECIMENS RECEIVED   A  Molecular test for MYC    GROSS DESCRIPTION   1 block from Massachusetts General Hospital  the archived specimen was retrieved  and reviewed for adequacy    SLIDE BLOCK DESCRIPTION    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID             TEST   MYC FISH ANALYSIS    INDICATION FOR TEST  Soft Tissue  Left Breast Areola  Angiosarcoma    SPECIMEN S  TESTED   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA   United States     FISH RESULTS   Fluorescence in situ hybridization of paraffin tumor tissue using a break apart  probe to the MYC locus showed     ISCN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  nomenclature  nuc ish  MYCx2  50     INTERPRETATION     NORMAL    NEGATIVE for MYC rearrangement     TEST INFORMATION   Rearrangement involving the MYC gene on 8q24 is present in approximately 5 10   of diffuse large B cell lymphomas  DLBCL  and has been associated with a poor  prognosis  MYC rearrangements are also present in Burkitt s lymphoma  These  rearrangements result in the constitutive expression of Myc and subsequent  binding of Enhancer Box sequences and histone acetyltransferase recruitment     Fluorescence in situ hybridization  FISH  using formalin fixed paraffin embedded  specimens has been shown to be an effective method for determining presence of  these translocations  Briefly  5 micron sections of formalin fixed  paraffin embedded tumor material were prepared and an H E section reviewed to  select regions for hybridization that contain a majority of tumor cells  A MYC  break apart probe  Vysis LSI MYC Dual Color  Break Apart Rearrangement Probe   was hybridized and used to calculate the number of cells out of 50 scored  containing a rearrangement  A MYC rearrangement is reported if more than 15  of  cells show split signals  CPT codes for this test   REMOVED_CASE_ID   morphometric analysis   in situ hybridization  each probe  manual  x 1     This test was developed and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Diagnostic Molecular Pathology Laboratory  It has not been cleared or  approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that  such clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical  purposes  Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has  established and verified the test s accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH internal address  Diagnostic Molecular Pathology Laboratory   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St   Warren 508  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID           Electronically Signed Out By  Jochen K Lennerz MD  PHD         PART   Molecular test for MYC       report_end  , No.
