imately 95  diffusely  dense lumpy white tan soft tissue and less than 5  yellow tan lobulated adipose  tissue with no discrete masses identified   Also received in the specimen container is an irregular fragment of tan  wrinkled grossly unremarkable skin  2 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm   with no discrete  lesions identified   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  perpendicular sections and skin fragment   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    2  frags each  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Ill defined retracted lesion with superior  inferior  anterior   and posterior margins  sequentially submitted from medial to lateral  multi  frags  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  perpendicular sections  2 frags each  RSS   Micro  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional lateral margin  2 frags each  RSS   Please note  Approximately 60  of the specimen to include the majority of the  retracted fibrous lesion is submitted   Specimen B  according to requisition and specimen container labeling and also  per sutures and ink placed by surgeon is received consistent with a left breast  excision specimen  However  the patient s clinical history on requisition  suggests the operation was a right breast re excision  Please note  The  surgeon  Dr  Rhei  was contacted by Dr  VanderLaan in regards to the  orientation of sutures placed and inking protocol  The specimen was confirmed  to be a RIGHT breast re excision   CASE NUMBER   REMOVED_CASE_ID    LM ag  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by William R Welch M D   on REMOVED_DATE  Amendment  1 by William R Welch M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE   report_end  , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Molecular Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH Analysis      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  W   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  53   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  YAW 9  BREAST ONC  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 23 57  Results To   Steven Jay Isakoff MD  PhD  Elena F  Brachtel MD    CLINICAL HISTORY   Breast Invasive Ductal Carcinoma    SPECIMENS RECEIVED   A  Molecular test for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     GROSS DESCRIPTION   1 block s  from Massachusetts General Hospital    SLIDE BLOCK DESCRIPTION    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID             TEST    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  FISH ANALYSIS    INDICATION FOR TEST  Breast Invasive Ductal Carcinoma    SPECIMEN S  TESTED   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA   United States     RESULTS     Fibroblast Growth Factor Receptor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   copy number analysis      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Reference Probe Copy Number Ratio  REMOVED_DATE    INTERPRETATION     The FISH data are consistent with NO amplification of the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene     TEST INFORMATION   Aberrations involving the fibroblast growth factor receptor 1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   gene have  been noted in tumors of multiple types  including certain lung  breast  ovarian   skeletal muscle  melanocytic and hematopoietic neoplasms   1  Amplification of  the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene was recently identified as a significant and common finding  22   by FISH  in a cohort of squamous cell carcinomas of the lung   2     The assay performed on this patient uses fluorescence in situ hybridization   FISH  on formalin fixed paraffin embedded tumor specimens to analyze  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene  amplification status  Briefly  5 micron sections of formalin fixed  paraffin embedded tumor material were prepared and an H E section reviewed to  select regions for hybridization that contain a majority of tumor cells  A  dual color FISH assay was performed using Bacterial Artificial Chromosome probe  CTD  REMOVED_CASE_ID  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   chromosome 8p   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  locus  home brew  and a copy number control   centromere 8  Abbott Vysis 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  or 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       Signal quantitation was used to generate a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  centromere 8 ratio   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  Centromere 8 ratios are interpreted as follows  REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered  borderline for amplification  REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE is considered low level amplification   and greater than REMOVED_DATE or clustered  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  signals that are too numerous to count  would be considered highly amplified  CPT codes for this assay are  REMOVED_CASE_ID  x 2     REFERENCES   1  Turner N and Grose R  Fibroblast growth factor signaling  from  development to cancer  Nature Reviews Cancer 10 116   REMOVED_CASE_ID     2  Weiss J  Sos  M  et al  Frequent and focal  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  amplification  associates with therapeutically tractable  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  dependency in squamous cell lung  cancer  Sci Transl Med 2 62  62ra93   REMOVED_CASE_ID       This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Center for Integrated Diagnostics  It has not been cleared or approved  by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that such  clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical purposes   Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA  88  this laboratory has established and  verified the test s accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MG