Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 05 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   WITH FOCAL SIGNET RING CELL FORMATION  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE DEEP RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE  2  METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 3 OF 19 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  Note  No definite blood vascular invasion is identified  Extranodal soft tissue extension is present in 2 of 3 positive lymph nodes    ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGINS  LEFT    FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Labeled  left breast and axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm oriented left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the 12 o clock position  The specimen includes a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tail  Overlying the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm skin ellipse  with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm nipple alveolar complex  located 2 8cm from the 12 o clock skin margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white  stellate  firm mass located in the upper outer quadrant  extending to within 0 2cm of the closest deep resection margin  and 1 5cm from the closest 2 o clock soft tissue margin  The mass extends to the base of the axillary tail  Apart from this mass  the remaining parenchyma shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  tan  fibrotic  rubbery  ill defined area  located in the upper inner quadrant  6 0cm from the 11 o clock margin  and 1 0cm from the closest deep margin  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The largest lymph node contains a firm  tan white cut surface  Section code  A  nipple B D tumor with deep resection margin E H tumor  representative sections I K fibrotic area L R lymph nodes Labeled  additional anterior margin  left  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable tan yellow  soft breast parenchyma  Entirely submitted in S W  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Barbara Ann Penn  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGINS  LEFT    report_end  , Yes.
