Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit Street  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  C   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  63   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location  WAC 835  NEUROLOGY ASSOC  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 09 20  Results To   Amel Karaa MD      FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   SKIN  STANDARD DISTAL LEG   PUNCH BIOPSY   Qualitative microscopic examination of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  5 immuno labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   revealed marked reduction of innervation of epidermis  Dermal structures such  as glands  hair follicles  and blood vessels were better innervated  consistent  with distal axonopathy of small cutaneous sensory axons  Quite a few axons had  swellings  considered a soft sign of axonopathy     Morphometric quantitation of epidermal nerve endings yielded a density of 89  neurites mm2 of skin surface area  at less than the 1st centile based on our  laboratory s age  sex  and race adjusted normative data series  Values at or  below the 5th centile are considered diagnostic for a small fiber axonopathy     These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by  the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not  been cleared or approved by the U  S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The  FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this  laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision          Electronically Signed Out By Anne Louise Oaklander MD  PHD           By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis   