Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 32 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT BREAST    BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I II III   EXTENDING TO AN INKED SURFACE ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  PREDOMINANTLY ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS AND FOCAL LACTATIONAL CHANGES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 30                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm area of cysts and fibrosis with a central 0 5cm area of calcification  This area abuts the margin  This area is submitted entirely in cassettes A through D  Representative sections of the remaining tissue are submitted in cassettes E through F  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   CYSTS AND FIBROSIS  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , No.
