Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Amend Addenda  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Consult material  Procedure Date   Ordering Provider  NANCY U LIN M D   CASE  BS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  TOOLE             Addended Report              Resident  Stephanie Schulte  M D   Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   CONSULT SLIDES FROM MASSACHUSETTS GENERAL HOSPITAL  BOSTON  MA   RIGHT BREAST  TWO EXCISIONS   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   9 12  REMOVED_CASE_ID     WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS   Apocrine cysts with calcifications   Note  By report  the targeted calcifications were not present in this  specimen  but were present in the additional tissue reported below    MEDIAL TISSUE TOWARDS NIPPLE   EXCISION   MICROINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA    0 1cm  only present in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    levels 2  3  and 4  and not present on level 1 or deeper levels used for  immunohistochemical studies    SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN  SITU  associated with columnar cell change with flat atypia  mucin  production  and calcifications  is present as a 0 4cm focus in one block   block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   levels examined  see note   Single cell necrosis is present   Additional small foci of columnar cell change with flat atypia are present in  blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Immunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results for  ADH  reviewed    Estrogen receptor POSITIVE  Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE  Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen  and progesterone receptors   The invasive carcinoma and the ADH are   0 1cm from the unoriented  margin   Note  The area of ADH is difficult to classify  ADH is favored due to  the predominant clinging pattern without definite architectural features to  support carcinoma in situ   The invasive carcinoma is very small and is only seen on some levels of  one block  Additional studies cannot be performed as the carcinoma is no  longer present on the deeper levels   This case was also reviewed by Dr  Andrea Richardson  Dr  Deborah  Dillon  and Dr  Jane Brock  who concur with this interpretation   This carcinoma would be classified as AJCC  6th edition   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID mic NX   RIGHT BREAST  RE EXCISION   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   10 17  REMOVED_CASE_ID     Biopsy site changes   Note  No residual carcinoma is seen   CLINICAL DATA   History  Right breast microcalcifications   Clinical Diagnosis  DCIS   TISSUE SUBMITTED   Consult slides   GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received from Massachusetts General Hospital  Pathology Department  55 Fruit  Street  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   are forty seven  47  glass slides  3 slides are  unstained    Thirty four  34  slides are labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and sublabeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   though    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   through   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   through   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    through   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   through   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   through   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  unstained  through   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  unstained     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ER     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PR  and   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     corresponding to A  right breast  medial tissue toward nipple  excision  3 5 x  2 6 x 1 5cm   B  right breast excision  4 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm   performed on  9 12 08  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient s  name   Thirteen  13  slides are labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and sublabeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   through    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   through   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    corresponding to a right breast  excision  4 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm   performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the  accompanying pathology report bearing the patient s name   By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she  personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated   of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es   related thereto   Final Diagnosis by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on  Thursday February 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 41 03PM  SURGICAL ADDENDUM   Five slides labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and sublabeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are received for review again   One of the H E slides was destained and restained with cytokeratin cocktail    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2   slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     In the area diagnosed as microinvasive lobular carcinoma  there is one  cytokeratin positive cell  The remaining approximately 50 cells are not  immunoreactive for cytokeratin   Although the majority of the luminal cells are positive for cytokeratin  there  are some negative luminal cells   In the surrounding tissue  there are atypical cells in ducts suggestive of  atypical lobular hyperplasia  These cells are also negative for cytokeratin   It is possible that these cells are a precursor lesion for the microinvasion   Therefore  although the absence of cytokeratin immunoreactivity in a carcinoma  using this particular antibody cocktail is unusual  the finding does not  exclude the diagnosis of microinvasive lobular carcinoma   Dr  Andrea Richardson and Dr  Deborah Dillon reviewed these slides and concur  with this interpretation   Addendum  1 by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on Wednesday  REMOVED_MONTH 11   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06 30 22PM   report_end  , No.
