epithelial layer in areas of invasive carcinoma and supports the diagnosis  An immunostain for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  was performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and highlights endothelial cells  An immunostain for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is non contributory  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast mastectomy   is a 30 x 18 x 4 5cm left mastectomy specimen with a 28 x 13cm overlying skin ellipse with a 4 x 3cm unremarkable nipple areolar complex  The skin is white and the specimen is oriented with a stitch designating 12 o clock  The anterior surface is inked blue and posterior surface is inked black and specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm firm tan ill demarcated centrally hemorrhagic mass which is 1 5cm from the closest posterior resection margin and 3cm from the closest anterior resection margin  The mass is located in the upper outer quadrant of the specimen  There is also a separate REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 7cm fibrotic area 4cm from the first mass  and located approximately in the midline of the specimen  The area of fibrosis is 5cm from the posterior resection margin and 3cm from the anterior resection margin and skin ellipse  The rest of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative section is submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest posterior resection margin to the 1st mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest anterior margin to the 1st mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the 1st mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the described fibrotic area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest posterior resection to the 2nd mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cross section of the nipple  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 03   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 10 30 32PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagn