Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report    Amended      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  A   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  49   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location  PAC  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 12 12  Results To   James F Markmann MD  PhD      AMENDMENTS  Amendment Reason  Modified Intra Operative Pathologist or Resident  Previous Signout Date  REMOVED_DATE 17 55    FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS     KIDNEY  ALLOGRAFT REMOVED_DATE MONTHS   NEPHRECTOMY   VENOUS THROMBOSIS WITH CORTICAL AND MEDULLARY INFARCTIONS    Note  Cortical and medullary infarctions are present by both gross and  microscopic examinations and associated with acute and subacute venous  thromboses  confirmed on elastic stains  Immunofluorescence for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID d is negative   Double immunohistochemical stains for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID d  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is an endothelial stain   were performed on multiple sections to assure that a negative  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID d stain was  interpreted on intact capillary endothelium  with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  staining   Although  substantial endothelial injury is present  sufficient intact capillaries were  identified to interpret the immunohistochemical  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID d staining as negative  There  is no interstitial inflammation  A few small arteries contained some intimal  hyperplasia  which has two possible interpretations  1  focal allograft  vasculopathy or 2  intimal hyperplasia that is donor derived  The venous  thrombosis is most likely secondary to the glomerular proteinuria  Contributing  factors may include the patient s pancreatitis  A coagulopathy cannot be  excluded  Acute cellular  acute antibody  or chronic alloantibody mediated  rejections are not present  There is no evidence of post transplant  lymphoproliferative disease     KIDNEY  ALLOGRAFT REMOVED_DATE MONTHS   EXPLORATORY LAPAROTOMY PRE NEPHRECTOMY BIOPSY   MARKED TUBULAR INJURY AND NECROSIS    Note  All frozen section diagnoses confirmed     PERIPANCREATIC SOFT TISSUE  EXPLORATORY LAPAROTOMY BIOPSY   FIBROUS TISSUE  NECROSIS  FIBRIN    Note  All frozen section diagnoses confirmed  Brown   Hopps stain for bacteria  is negative  There is no evidence of post transplant lymphoproliferative  disease     PERIPANCREATIC SOFT TISSUE  BIOPSY   FIBROUS TISSUE  NECROSIS  FIBRIN    Note  Brown   Hopps stain for bacteria is negative  There is no evidence of  post transplant lymphoproliferative disease      POSSIBLE LYMPH NODE   BIOPSY   FIBROFATTY TISSUE  FIBRIN  NECROSIS      Note  Lymph node not identified  Brown   Hopps stain for bacteria is negative   There is no evidence of post transplant lymphoproliferative disease        Electronically Signed Out By Rex Neal Smith MD  PhD           By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   KIDNEY BIOPSY FROZEN SUBMITTED IN  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     Diffuse tubular necrosis  small artery fibrin     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2   PERIPANCREATIC TISSUE    Fibrous tissue with necrosis   fibrin     Note  This case was amended to add intraoperative diagnosis staff resident     Rex Neal Smith MD  PhD    CLINICAL HISTORY  49 year old female who received preemptive kidney pancreas transplant on  10 14  REMOVED_CASE_ID   The patient initially had an uncomplicated course but presented with  renal graft dysfunction  Biopsy on REMOVED_DATE suggested collapsing glomerulopathy   The patient s creatinine continued to rise  She also had evidence of an EBV  infection and PET scan  had a single hot spot in the area of the pancreas  Pancreas biopsy showed no  evidence of rejection and no evidence of PTLD  Over the last few days the  patient deteriorated with increasing abdominal pain  The day of surgery the  patient had evidence of diffuse peritonitis  Differential of possible leak post  pancreas biopsy versus C  difficile  colitis versus a renal graft inflammation  Brought to the Operating Room for  exploration and with the hope of biopsying the kidney and potentially biopsying  the pancreas     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  LEFT KIDNEY ALLOGRAFT BIOPSY  B  PERIPANCREATIC SOFT TISSUE BIOPSY  C  PERI PANCREATIC TISSUE BIOPSY  D  KIDNEY ALLOGRAFT  E    LYMPH NODE BIOPSY    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN     A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  kidney biopsy  frozen  is  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm core biopsy  FX 1 submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two more cores received  for permanents measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm each     B  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   peripancreatic tissue   measuring  1 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm FX 2  submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One more fragment received for  permanents measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received are 3 containers which are each labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      C  Received fresh  labeled  peripancreatic tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  aggregate of pink tan necrotic appearing tissue which is submitted in toto in  cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      D  Received fresh  labeled  kidney allograft   is a 452 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm fragmented kidney  The vascular and ureteral margins are cut flush with the  exposed surface of the kidney  The external surface is red pink with minimal  adhesions and a area of gray white punctate discoloration  The specimen is  bivalved to reveal dark red congested cut surfaces with a small pelvis and  calyceal system  The urothelium is gray white and glistening  The renal  parenchyma is congested red brown with 7 long to medullary pyramids  The  corticomedullary junction is ill defined with the cortex measuring up to 1 3cm   There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm gray white ill defined to wedge shaped lesion  subjacent to the capsule  Corticomedullary tissue is submitted for electron  microscopy and a portion is saved frozen in Warren 5  Half of the specimen is  saved in saline  Gross photographs are taken  The branches of the hilar  vasculature appear to have multiple areas of clot or thrombus formation   Representative sections are submitted as follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Vascular and ureteral margins  en face    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Punctate gray white area    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Renal pelvis    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Corticomedullary junction    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gray white wedge shaped lesion with overlying capsule    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Congested hilar vasculature    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Corticomedullary junction    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional    E  Received fresh  labeled  rule out lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  tan pink nodular tissue possibly representing a lymph node which is submitted in  toto in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID          PART A  LEFT KIDNEY ALLOGRAFT BIOPSY  PART B  PERIPANCREATIC SOFT TISSUE BIOPSY  PART C  PERI PANCREATIC TISSUE BIOPSY  PART D  KIDNEY ALLOGRAFT  PART E    LYMPH NODE BIOPSY       report_end  , No.
