t carcinoma and harbors  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   mutation     Physical Exam  The right breast at 10 o clock showed a 0 6cm non tender   well defined  ovoid  firm and mobile nodule     Ultrasound was used to evaluate the lesion and showed a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  lesion that was  well defined  ovoid  solid  homogeneously  hypoechoic and  without significant internal vascularity     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation     2 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles with local anesthesia and  without complications   2 slides were stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by Darcy Kerr  Fellow     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were not discussed with the  patient  Michelle Specht  MD was notified of the preliminary results by e mail  at 12 05p m       The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Rosemary H Tambouret MD on REMOVED_DATE 16 42       CLINICAL HISTORY  New right breast mass at 10 o clock         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT  Received 2 slides in ETOH  Received 2 air dried  slides  Received 4cc s of clear colorless fluid  One SurePath slide made           Specime